title: "sc-hop: harden data pool against DOS vectors"

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      Follow-up to #11662 hardening the HOP node service:

      - Aggregate cross-account bandwidth bucket in `RateLimiter` — a coordinated
        set of authorized accounts can no longer saturate the pool by each
        staying within its per-account limit.
      - Per-sender rate-limiter map bounded at `max_tracked_senders`; when full,
        the sender with the most remaining capacity is evicted so exhausted
        senders stay tracked.
      - Crate-level `MAX_DATA_SIZE` (2 MiB) hard cap on a single submission,
        enforced in the pool independently of the runtime-reported
        `max_promotion_size`. `HopError::DataTooLarge`'s limit field widens
        from `u32` to `u64` accordingly.
      - `HopDataPool::new` rejects `max_size`, `max_user_size`, and both
        `bandwidth_burst` values that are smaller than the accounted cost of a
        max-size blob at full recipient fan-out — new `HopError::InvalidConfig`.

  - audience: Node Operator
    description: |
      New flags: `--hop-global-bandwidth-per-min-mib` (1024),
      `--hop-global-bandwidth-burst-mib` (2048), `--hop-max-rate-limit-senders`
      (100 000).

crates:
  - name: sc-hop
    bump: major
